<Doc
  title="Privacy Policy"
  kicker="Legal"
  updated="October 8, 2026"
  description="What FutureClarity Technologies collects when you book a free audit or contact us, how we use it, who helps us run things, and your choices."
>
  <p>
    FutureClarity Technologies ("we", "us") builds custom dashboards, automations, websites and app
    fixes for local businesses. This policy explains what we collect through
    futureclaritytechnologies.com and in our work, how we use it, and the choices you have. If
    anything here is unclear, email <a href="mailto:beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com">beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com</a>
    or call <a href="tel:+18189397964">(818) 939-7964</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>When you book a free audit or contact us:</strong> your name, your business's name, the
      email or phone number you give us, your website or app if you mention them, what you tell us
      you need, the services you pick, the price range the site showed you, and which ad or website
      brought you to us, if any (see "In your browser" below).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>When you call, text or email us:</strong> your contact details and what you send.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>When you visit the site:</strong> our host processes standard technical details, such as
      your IP address, browser type and the pages you request, to deliver the site and protect it
      from abuse. We don't use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>In your browser:</strong> we use your browser's own storage, not cookies. While you
      book on a computer, the details from step 1 are kept there so step 2 can fill them in; they're
      removed when you send your request. After you send a request, a note that you did is kept
      until you close the tab, so the form doesn't ask twice. And if you arrive from one of our ads
      or from another website, we keep which one for up to 30 days (the ad's campaign tags, an ad
      click ID if the ad adds one, or the other site's name) and include it with your request, so we
      know which ads work. It stays on this site: we don't use it to follow you anywhere else, and
      we don't send it to the ad companies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>About businesses we might work with:</strong> we use publicly available business
      information, such as business listings, public websites and Google reviews, to find local
      businesses that could use our services. We keep business contact details and notes about our
      outreach.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to you, set up and run your free audit, prepare your quote, and provide the work you hire us for.</li>
    <li>To contact businesses about our services, by phone, in person, or by email with an easy way to opt out.</li>
    <li>To keep the site and our records secure, and to meet our legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>We don't sell your personal information</strong>, and we don't share it with anyone for
    advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Calls and texts</h2>
  <p>
    If you give us your phone number when you book or contact us, we may call or text you about your
    request, sometimes using automated tools. We don't send marketing texts without your permission.
    How often we text depends on your request. Reply STOP to any text from us and we'll stop texting
    you, or HELP for help. Message and data rates may apply. See our <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> for
    more about texts.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We don't share mobile numbers or text-message consent with anyone for their marketing.</strong>
    Your text-message opt-in and consent are never shared with or sold to third parties. The
    providers that carry our messages handle them only to deliver them.
  </p>

  <h2>Who helps us run things</h2>
  <p>We use a few service providers, who handle information only to provide their service to us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the website and protects it from abuse.</li>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> stores audit requests and our client and outreach records.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> serves the site's fonts, so Google receives your IP address and browser details when a page loads.</li>
    <li>Our <strong>email and phone providers</strong> carry the messages we send and receive.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information when the law requires it, to protect our rights or someone's
    safety, or to a new owner if our business is sold or merged, who would be bound by this policy.
  </p>

  <h2>When we build for a client</h2>
  <p>
    Our dashboards and automations handle our clients' customer information, such as names and
    phone numbers for booking reminders. We handle it only to provide the services, following the
    client's instructions. The client's own privacy policy covers how they use it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Ask to see, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you, or tell us to stop
      contacting you, by emailing <a href="mailto:beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com">beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com</a>
      or calling <a href="tel:+18189397964">(818) 939-7964</a>. We'll reply promptly, and within 45 days.
    </li>
    <li>Every sales email from us includes a way to opt out, and we honor it.</li>
    <li>We won't treat you differently for making any of these requests.</li>
    <li>
      California residents: we don't share personal information with other companies for their own
      marketing (California Civil Code § 1798.83).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control</h2>
  <p>
    We don't track you across other websites, no other company collects information about what you
    do on our site for its own use, and we don't sell or share personal information. So there is
    nothing for a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal to switch off. Your browser can send
    them; nothing changes.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep audit requests, client records and outreach notes as long as we need them for the work,
    our records and our legal obligations, then delete them. You can ask us to delete yours sooner.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses HTTPS, the database that holds audit requests is locked so only our team can read
    it, and access is limited to the people who need it. No system is perfectly secure, but we take
    reasonable steps to protect what you share with us.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our site and services are for businesses. They aren't directed to children, and we don't
    knowingly collect information from anyone under 16.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When we change this policy, we'll post the new version here with a new date. If a change affects
    how we use information you've already given us, we'll ask first.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
